---
const cards = [
  {
    tag: "Agent traffic",
    title: "Autonomous agents don't behave like your other traffic",
    body: "Tool-call fan-outs fire five to thirty parallel requests in under fifty milliseconds, with near-zero dwell time between a response and the next dependent call. A static per-IP limiter can't tell that apart from an attack — it just drops things.",
    points: [
      "Classifies the caller from request signals (Agent, StandardApi, Human, Unknown)",
      "Fingerprints repeat callers internally, never exposed to the caller",
      "Everything else passes through untouched — no evaluation, no record",
    ],
  },
  {
    tag: "API keys",
    title: "Any caller can get a key with a real limit attached",
    body: "Issue a key, attach a requests-per-minute policy, and bufferq enforces it — atomically, under concurrency, with no race between the request that got through and the one that didn't. Callers that are over the limit get a token back, not a dead end.",
    points: [
      "Fixed per-minute windows — a window resets, it doesn't just keep rolling forward",
      "A denied request gets a poll token, not just a 429 and silence",
      'The caller asks "can I come in now?" and gets a real answer',
    ],
  },
];
---

<div class="border-b border-rule">
  <div class="section-wide py-24">
    <h2 class="h2-display">Two different problems, one gate</h2>
    <p class="lede mt-4">
      Both are live in bufferq today — the same classification and policy engine, pointed at
      different traffic.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-11 flex flex-wrap gap-5">
      {
        cards.map((c) => (
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-[1_1_440px] rounded-[6px] border border-rule bg-paper-2 p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="eyebrow">{c.tag}</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="block h-[7px] w-[7px] rounded-full bg-status-grant" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="mt-4.5 text-2xl font-semibold leading-snug tracking-tight text-ink">{c.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3.5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">{c.body}</p>
            <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-3 border-t border-rule-2 pt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
              {c.points.map((p) => (
                <div class="flex gap-3">
                  <span class="mono text-neutral-2">—</span>
                  <span>{p}</span>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
